        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04 16:21:32.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04 17:45:50.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 lod: keep the pool of a striped dir in its LMV",
        "message": "LU-21061 lod: keep the pool of a striped dir in its LMV\n\nA striped directory made by lfs mkdir with -p POOL, or with a layout\nin a tree whose default LMV names POOL, has its stripes on the MDTs\nof POOL, but nothing of its own records the pool: the lmv_pool_name\nfield of its LMV stays empty and it gets no default LMV.  A later\nsplit, automatic or by hand, takes the new stripes from any MDT.\n\nIn lod_ah_init(), take a pool given for the directory, also the one\nof its tree that clients fill in, as its own, and write it into the\nLMV in lod_prep_lmv_md(); a replayed create keeps the pool of its\nLMV.  In lod_dir_declare_layout_split(), use the pool of the LMV\nbefore the ones of the default LMV and of the request, and keep it in\nthe new layout.  In lod_dir_layout_shrink(), start from the current\nLMV, so that a merge keeps the pool too.  Keep the pool in the LMV\nheader conversions of LFSCK.  Return the pool with\nLL_IOC_LMV_GETSTRIPE, so that lfs getdirstripe shows it, and clear it\nin llapi for a directory without a layout.  A plain directory has no\nLMV: it keeps a pool for its splits only through its default LMV.\n\nAdd ost-pools test 35m.\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I5e25de471530e955fb5486b4b06856ed7fe45bfd\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
